1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Reviewing a protein variant requires more than a model score.

2
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:11,983
BioPilot Atlas brings the task, constraints, recorded tool decisions, and candidate evidence into one
review workspace.

3
00:00:12,134 --> 00:00:19,589
This local draft uses edited captures of saved real results, with disclosed synthetic narration, not a fresh
model run.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,563
The task concerns a public Lipase A reference, using full reference, one based positions.

5
00:00:26,713 --> 00:00:30,836
The complete reference sequence is the registered scoring context.

6
00:00:30,986 --> 00:00:34,237
Important catalytic sites remain protected.

7
00:00:34,387 --> 00:00:40,707
Here a separate offline check validates the declared numbering and substitution with the same product
guards.

8
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:44,539
That check does not change this saved scientific run.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,894
The decision trace opens the original public tool record.

10
00:00:49,044 --> 00:00:54,687
Muse Spark requested target validation and then the permitted scoring tool through MCP.

11
00:00:54,837 --> 00:01:00,176
Each recorded step exposes its short reason, bounded arguments, and result.

12
00:01:00,326 --> 00:01:06,249
Local ESM computed the sequence preferences, and code produced the common ranking.

13
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:12,252
Moving between saved steps only changes the view; it sends no provider request.

14
00:01:12,402 --> 00:01:15,351
No private chain of thought is displayed.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,678
Changing the input check to a protected serine substitution produces a clear refusal.

16
00:01:25,828 --> 00:01:30,492
The code enforces the constraint even when a user asks for that change.

17
00:01:30,642 --> 00:01:36,225
Declaring mature sequence numbering also requires correction rather than a guessed offset.

18
00:01:36,375 --> 00:01:41,304
These are separate local guard interactions, not new Meta responses.

19
00:01:41,454 --> 00:01:45,388
The saved candidate scores and ranks remain unchanged.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,988
The overview starts with the leading candidates instead of a wall of identifiers.

21
00:01:55,138 --> 00:02:00,782
A researcher can inspect selected candidates side by side and export the recorded table.

22
00:02:00,932 --> 00:02:06,210
Scores, positions, and original ranks are rendered directly from the artifact.

23
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:10,843
Selection does not create a new ranking or establish an improvement.

24
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:19,777
ESM preferences are not T fifty, activity, solubility, melting temperature, or proof of retained function.

25
00:02:19,927 --> 00:02:22,946
Unknown geometry remains unavailable.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,369
A frozen protocol now records two arms that actually ran.

27
00:02:29,519 --> 00:02:34,832
Local guards answered six of six; the Meta model, five of six.

28
00:02:34,982 --> 00:02:39,551
Its one miss accepted a variant whose reference residue it never checked.

29
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:43,715
Code refused it, and the manual arm was never run.

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,207
Inspect the recorded model, score policy, and source hashes.

31
00:02:49,357 --> 00:02:54,102
Actual billing remains unknown and biological efficacy remains unestablished.

32
00:02:54,252 --> 00:02:59,588
BioPilot supports human review with guarded tools; earlier work stays credited.

